            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0362" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.11L5232/568: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-11T19:00:00-04:00">May 11, 1936—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>49. Your 139, May 9, 2 p.m., regarding sabotage claims. Department is informed
                    that German Agent does not have instructions authorizing him to take initiative
                    in requesting adjournment, but does have instructions authorizing him not to
                    object to such adjournment.</p>
                <p>This does not appear to be in accord with information contained in your cable to
                    the effect that Goering is instructing German Agent to request that the hearings
                    be adjourned and had expressed the hope that American Agent would be helpful in
                    that regard.</p>
                <p>Under these circumstances, unless German Agent does take the initiative, it is
                    presumed that the arguments will proceed as scheduled on May 12.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
